When caret-color is auto, Ladybird keeps auto as the computed value and
reads the element’s own color wherever the caret is painted or
getComputedStyle() resolves it. The other engines resolve it at use the
same way. Blink keeps caret-color as a StyleAutoColor in ComputedStyle,
and CaretDisplayItemClient resolves it at paint with LayoutObject::
ResolveColor(GetCSSPropertyCaretColor()). WebKit’s CaretBase::
computeCaretColor() checks caretColor().isAuto() when it picks the color
to paint. And Gecko keeps nsStyleUI::mCaretColor as a StyleColorOrAuto,
and nsIFrame::GetCaretColorAt() resolves it at paint time, through
GetVisitedDependentColor().
